mehr@oskar.uchicago.edu (David Mehringer) writes:

>So, has anyone gotten an artifact by sacrificing humans when
>playing chaotic characters?  The time I was talking about was
>when I sacrificed at least a dozen Kops (probably more).  I got
>nothing of value (that I could tell) for my eforts.

I have never received an artifact after having sacrificed a human,
(although I haven't sacrificed humans very often). As I said before
though, unless the spoilers are incorrect you did increase your luck
+2 each time you sacrificed (up to a max. +10 without a luckstone).

In any case, receiving an artifact and increasing your luck are two
different issues. I once got Stormbringer on level 1 by sacrificing
a newt corpse. There's no way the newt increased my luck, they're only
one step up from grid bugs on the wimpiness scale. So I would conclude
that with each sacrifice you have a chance of getting an artifact 
(calculated from various factors which probably include luck). Once
that has been determined then your God evaluates the size and quality of
your sacrifice and decides whether to increase your luck or not.

To really clarify things I think you need to look at the code (I haven't
done so, so I can't say for certain that the above is 100% accurate).

